<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>
      {{ page.title | escape }}
      | Research Portfolio
    </title>
    <meta name="description" content="{{ page.description | escape }}">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#080808">
    <meta property="og:type" content="website">
    <meta property="og:title" content="{{ page.title | escape }}">
    <meta property="og:description" content="{{ page.description | escape }}">
    <meta property="og:image" content="{{ '/assets/img/portfolio/doris-portrait.webp' | absolute_url }}">
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="Portrait of Doris Wang">
    <link rel="canonical" href="{{ page.url | absolute_url }}">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="{{ '/assets/img/portfolio/doris-mark.png' | relative_url }}">
    <link rel="preload" href="{{ '/assets/fonts/portfolio/dm-sans.woff2' | relative_url }}" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/assets/css/portfolio.css' | relative_url | bust_file_cache }}">
    <script defer src="{{ '/assets/js/portfolio.js' | relative_url | bust_file_cache }}"></script>
  </head>
  <body id="top">
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="site-header">
      <nav class="header-inner" aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a class="wordmark" href="{{ '/' | relative_url }}" aria-label="Doris Wang, home">
          <span class="wordmark-initials" aria-hidden="true">DW</span>
          <span>Doris Wang</span>
        </a>
        <div class="nav-links">
          <a href="#research">Research</a>
          <a href="#about">About me</a>
          <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
        </div>
        <a class="nav-cv" href="{{ '/cv/' | relative_url }}">CV</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main id="main">
      <div class="research-area">
        <section
          class="research content-width"
          id="research"
          aria-labelledby="research-title"
          data-pgg-source="{{ '/pgg-feasibility/data.json' | relative_url }}"
        >
          <header class="section-heading">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow section-kicker">Research agenda</p>
              <h1 id="research-title">How do rules shape strategic behavior?</h1>
              <p>
                I study strategic interaction under incomplete information. The central question is how the rules of a market or organization change
                the way participants use private information. My current public goods experiment studies this through communication and costly
                enforcement. The projects that follow carry the same question into group choice and supply chain bargaining.
              </p>
            </div>
            <nav class="research-jumps" aria-label="On this page">
              <a href="#public-goods">1. Monitor action</a>
              <a href="#project-twins">2. Hold information fixed</a>
              <a href="#more-projects">3. Change capability</a>
              <a href="#research-horizon">4. Design the institution</a>
            </nav>
          </header>

          <ol class="research-program" aria-label="Research logic">
            <li><strong>Signal</strong><span>What information enters the conversation?</span></li>
            <li><strong>Rule</strong><span>What do actors know about monitoring and enforcement?</span></li>
            <li><strong>Allocation</strong><span>Who can use the information, and who gains bargaining power?</span></li>
            <li><strong>Outcome</strong><span>Does the group coordinate, choose well, or shift surplus?</span></li>
          </ol>

          <article class="feature" id="public-goods" aria-labelledby="pgg-title">
            <div class="feature-copy">
              <p class="eyebrow">Monitoring and enforcement</p>
              <h2 id="pgg-title">Can cheap talk improve the timing of punishment?</h2>
              <p>
                In round 10 of a public goods game I ran with 4 AI agents, P4 asked everyone to contribute 5 tokens and then put in 10. Choose a round
                and a player to place the message beside the action. The current experiment asks whether a disclosed language warning improves group
                earnings when it is added to the same history rule.
              </p>
              <div class="feature-links">
                <a class="solid-link" href="{{ '/pgg-feasibility/' | relative_url }}">Open the interactive study</a>
                <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/dorisduowang/pgg-feasibility">Code &amp; data</a>
                <a class="text-link" href="{{ '/projects/punishment_on_demand/' | relative_url }}">Earlier simulation</a>
              </div>
            </div>
            <figure class="pgg-figure">
              <div class="pgg-figure-header">
                <h3>Mean contribution per agent</h3>
              </div>
              <div class="pgg-canvas">
                <canvas id="pgg-chart" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
                <img
                  class="pgg-fallback"
                  src="{{ '/pgg-feasibility/figures/trajectory.png' | relative_url }}"
                  alt="Mean contributions across all 15 rounds. The highest mean was 10 tokens."
                  loading="lazy"
                >
              </div>
              <div class="round-panel" hidden>
                <div class="round-input">
                  <button class="round-play" type="button" aria-label="Play rounds"><span aria-hidden="true">▶</span></button>
                  <input id="round-input" type="range" min="1" max="15" value="10" step="1" aria-label="Select game round">
                  <span class="round-position" aria-hidden="true">10 / 15</span>
                </div>
                <output class="round-detail" for="round-input"></output>
                <div class="pgg-agents">
                  <p class="pgg-agents-heading"><strong>Individual contributions</strong> <span>of 20 tokens</span></p>
                  <ul data-pgg-agents aria-label="Individual contributions in tokens"></ul>
                  <div class="pgg-message" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
                    <p data-pgg-message-label></p>
                    <blockquote data-pgg-message></blockquote>
                  </div>
                  <p data-pgg-next></p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <figcaption>
                <span class="active-key" aria-hidden="true"></span> Shaded rounds mark when the history-based punishment rule was active.
              </figcaption>
            </figure>
          </article>

          {% assign grail = site.data.portfolio | where: 'figure', 'twins' | first %}
          <article class="feature grail-feature" id="project-twins" aria-labelledby="grail-title">
            <div class="feature-copy">
              <p class="eyebrow">Information aggregation</p>
              <h2 id="grail-title">Does the same evidence produce a different group decision?</h2>
              <p>
                The public goods game pairs talk with individual action. GRAIL moves the same question to a team. I designed 20 matched deliberations
                with 5 AI agents. Each agent received a fixed private report. The group then discussed the evidence and chose a city.
              </p>
              <div class="feature-links">
                <a class="text-link" href="{{ grail.url | escape }}">Read the public GRAIL protocol</a>
              </div>
            </div>
            <dl class="grail-design" aria-label="GRAIL study design">
              <div>
                <dt>What changes</dt>
                <dd>Who sits on each team.</dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt>What stays fixed</dt>
                <dd>The report each seat receives and the information made public.</dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt>What I compare</dt>
                <dd>The facts each team discusses, participation inside the group, and the final city.</dd>
              </div>
            </dl>
          </article>

          {% capture fomc_feature %}
          {% assign fomc = site.data.portfolio | where: 'figure', 'fomc' | first %}
          <article class="feature market-feature" id="fomc" aria-labelledby="fomc-title">
            <div class="feature-copy">
              <h2 id="fomc-title">{{ fomc.title | escape }}</h2>
              <p>{{ fomc.description | escape }}</p>
              <ol class="event-sequence" aria-label="Temporal validation study design">
                <li><strong>2 days before</strong><span>Collect GDELT news metadata.</span></li>
                <li><strong>Meeting day</strong><span>Anchor the event date. Use the minutes once released for the text comparison.</span></li>
                <li><strong>Next 5 trading days</strong><span>Measure realized S&amp;P 500 volatility.</span></li>
              </ol>
              <div class="feature-links">
                <a class="solid-link" href="{{ fomc.url | escape }}">{{ fomc.link | escape }}</a>
              </div>
              <p class="validation-note">The current branch reserves later meetings for holdout validation.</p>
            </div>
            <figure class="market-figure" data-market-chart>
              {% assign initial_lag = fomc.lags | where: 'primary', true | first %}
              <p class="eyebrow">Earlier analysis · 33 meetings</p>
              <h3>How much did the timing matter?</h3>
              <div class="market-plot-heading">
                <p class="market-axis-label">Pearson correlation (r)</p>
                <p class="market-hint" data-market-hint hidden>Choose a day for details</p>
              </div>
              <div class="market-plot">
                <div class="market-ticks" aria-hidden="true"><span>0.6</span><span>0.3</span><span>0</span></div>
                <div class="market-gridlines" aria-hidden="true"></div>
                <ol class="market-bars" role="list" aria-label="Correlation for each day relative to the meeting">
                  {% for lag in fomc.lags %}
                    {% assign correlation = lag.r | round: 2 %}
                    <li class="market-bar" style="--lag-height: {{ lag.r | divided_by: 0.6 | times: 100 }}%">
                      <button
                        class="market-select"
                        type="button"
                        aria-label="{{ lag.label | escape }}, Pearson r {{ correlation }}"
                        aria-pressed="{% if lag.primary %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
                        aria-controls="fomc-reading"
                        data-market-day="{{ lag.label | escape }}"
                        data-market-r="{{ correlation }}"
                        data-market-summary="{{ lag.explanation | escape }}"
                        disabled
                      >
                        <span class="market-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <span class="market-day">{{ lag.day | escape }}</span>
                        <strong class="market-value">{{ correlation }}</strong>
                      </button>
                    </li>
                  {% endfor %}
                </ol>
              </div>
              <p class="market-day-label">Days relative to the meeting</p>
              <div class="market-detail" id="fomc-reading" role="status" aria-atomic="true">
                <div class="market-detail-heading">
                  <strong data-market-selected-day>{{ initial_lag.label | escape }}</strong>
                  <span data-market-selected-r>r = {{ initial_lag.r | round: 2 }}</span>
                </div>
                <p data-market-selected-summary>{{ initial_lag.explanation | escape }}</p>
              </div>
              <figcaption>
                For each day, the analysis correlates GDELT news similarity to the eventual minutes with post-meeting S&amp;P 500 volatility. The 33
                meetings span March 2015 to March 2019. <a href="{{ fomc.baseline_source | escape }}">View the source data</a>.
              </figcaption>
            </figure>
          </article>
          {% endcapture %}

          <div class="work-heading" id="more-projects">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">The next institutional margin</p>
              <h2>From team composition to bargaining power</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter projects by topic" hidden>
              <button type="button" data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All</button>
              <button type="button" data-filter="cooperation" aria-pressed="false">Cooperation</button>
              <button type="button" data-filter="information" aria-pressed="false">Information</button>
              <button type="button" data-filter="operations" aria-pressed="false">Operations</button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="visually-hidden" id="filter-status" aria-live="polite"></p>
          <div class="work-grid">
            {% assign other_projects = site.data.portfolio | where: 'group', 'core' %}
            {% for project in other_projects %}
              <article
                class="work-card"
                data-core-project
                data-topic="{{ project.topic }}"
                aria-labelledby="project-{{ project.figure }}"
              >
                <div class="work-copy">
                  <h3 id="project-{{ project.figure }}">{{ project.title | escape }}</h3>
                  <p>{{ project.description | escape }}</p>
                </div>
                <details class="work-details">
                  <summary class="work-toggle" aria-label="Study details for {{ project.title | escape }}">
                    <span class="work-toggle-label">Question, data and method <span class="work-toggle-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></span>
                  </summary>
                  <dl class="work-detail-list">
                    <div>
                      <dt>Research question</dt>
                      <dd>{{ project.details.question | escape }}</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                      <dt>Data</dt>
                      <dd>{{ project.details.data | escape }}</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                      <dt>Methods</dt>
                      <dd>{{ project.details.methods | escape }}</dd>
                    </div>
                  </dl>
                </details>
                <div class="work-action">
                  <a
                    class="text-link"
                    href="{% if project.url contains '://' %}{{ project.url }}{% else %}{{ project.url | relative_url }}{% endif %}"
                  >
                    {{- project.link | escape -}}
                  </a>
                </div>
              </article>
            {% endfor %}
          </div>

          <section class="research-horizon" id="research-horizon" aria-labelledby="research-horizon-title">
            <p class="eyebrow">Long-term direction</p>
            <h2 id="research-horizon-title">Markets and organizations where AI agents act for people and firms</h2>
            <p>
              The next problem is not whether an agent is intelligent. It is which rules make its information useful without giving the strongest
              agent control over the outcome. AI systems will hold private information and negotiate across a network. Some will also learn how
              enforcement works. I want institutions that preserve coordination under those conditions.
            </p>
          </section>

          <div class="work-heading" id="other-work">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">Other work</p>
              <h2>Communication and financial markets</h2>
            </div>
          </div>
          {{ fomc_feature }}

          <div class="work-heading">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">Earlier work</p>
              <h2>Models, measurement, and audit</h2>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="work-grid">
            {% assign earlier_projects = site.data.portfolio | where: 'group', 'earlier' %}
            {% for project in earlier_projects %}
              <article class="work-card" data-topic="{{ project.topic }}" aria-labelledby="project-{{ project.figure }}">
                <div class="work-copy">
                  <h3 id="project-{{ project.figure }}">{{ project.title | escape }}</h3>
                  <p>{{ project.description | escape }}</p>
                </div>
                <details class="work-details">
                  <summary class="work-toggle" aria-label="Study details for {{ project.title | escape }}">
                    <span class="work-toggle-label">Question, data and method <span class="work-toggle-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></span>
                  </summary>
                  <dl class="work-detail-list">
                    <div>
                      <dt>Research question</dt>
                      <dd>{{ project.details.question | escape }}</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                      <dt>Data</dt>
                      <dd>{{ project.details.data | escape }}</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                      <dt>Methods</dt>
                      <dd>{{ project.details.methods | escape }}</dd>
                    </div>
                  </dl>
                </details>
                <div class="work-action">
                  <a
                    class="text-link"
                    href="{% if project.url contains '://' %}{{ project.url }}{% else %}{{ project.url | relative_url }}{% endif %}"
                  >
                    {{- project.link | escape -}}
                  </a>
                </div>
              </article>
            {% endfor %}
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>

      <section class="about" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
        <div class="about-inner content-width">
          <div class="about-copy">
            <p class="eyebrow section-kicker">About me</p>
            <h2 id="about-title">Hi, I’m Doris.</h2>
            <p>
              I’m an M.A. student in <a href="https://macss.uchicago.edu/">Computational Social Science (Economics)</a> at the University of Chicago.
              I received my B.Sc. in Political Economy from King’s College London.
            </p>
            <p>
              I study strategic interaction under incomplete information. My current public goods experiment asks whether communication can improve
              the timing of costly enforcement. The next project holds private reports fixed and changes the team. My operations work holds firm roles
              fixed and changes agent capability. The broader agenda is institutional design for settings in which AI agents hold information and act
              for people or firms.
            </p>
            <div class="about-links">
              <a class="text-link" href="{{ '/cv/' | relative_url }}">Curriculum vitae</a>
              <a class="text-link" href="{{ '/publications/' | relative_url }}">Publications</a>
              <a class="text-link" href="{{ '/teaching/' | relative_url }}">Teaching</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="about-photo-spread">
